# rel_split arguments that reproduce the golden split of sel_ngc_rel.
# sel_ngc's alignment stub is a STRING -- the case that broke rel_split's
# un-.if-0 handling. Restore the monolith from d32e854^ (5138d8f works too:
# only that commit's .c is the bad draft, its .s is fine).
# rel_rematch CANNOT re-split this module: run_split() never passes
# --include, and saved_inc only re-adds includes to pure-C files, so the
# group files come back non-compiling. Use rel_split directly with these.
#
# usage: python tools/rel_split.py sel_ngc_rel $(grep -v "^#" tools/rel_split_args/sel_ngc_rel.args)

